 contains © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL-1.0","aliases":[],"authors":["Open Landmarks contributors"],"artisticLicense":"CC-BY-4.0","spatialDataLicense":"ODbL-1.0","licenseScope":"CC BY applies to original artistic contributions only; ODbL applies to OSM-derived spatial data. Reference photographs retain their own licenses.","review":{"status":"pending","reviewer":null,"checks":{}},"modelingNotes":["Mapped 19-part plans retain the open internal courts, circular office ring, 20/31 m stepped wings and 68 m central archive tower.","Selected Commons river-front and Eiffel Tower photographs establish the white facade bands, dense rectangular glazing and raised tower crown; glazing uses the project light-blue material instead of photographic black reflections.","Three unheighted named studios lie inside the mapped 10 m interior base; they are not invented as taller volumes.","Named 15 m Studio 104 and Auditorium footprints override the coarse overlapping 20 m front-wing outline; this exposes their lower roofs rather than burying them beneath the parent cap.","The shallow mapped auditorium dome remains structural blue glazing; other wall=no glass roofs are thin coverings rather than full-height solid blocks.","Window bays are original map-scale simplifications at 18 m ring spacing and 6 m tower spacing. Rooftop lettering, equipment and facade posters are omitted."],"source":{"url":"/objects/d13c9dcbf03c675f77e6052806fb0e3c0595dadaec8003e8a2d70eb89f08fe57/source.blend.gz","bytes":222243,"sha256":"d13c9dcbf03c675f77e6052806fb0e3c0595dadaec8003e8a2d70eb89f08fe57"},"spatialSource":{"url":"/objects/609faf6160889d2527d70a9ace722ee198aeacfeb2b7de310e82c733e39da834/spatial-source.json","bytes":42692,"sha256":"609faf6160889d2527d70a9ace722ee198aeacfeb2b7de310e82c733e39da834"},"preview":{"url":"/objects/3040fc01cf7341edf37e0c177cacd00cd6be9b766b6ddd7e6de3cfe38e8baf27/preview.webp","bytes":11570,"sha256":"3040fc01cf7341edf37e0c177cacd00cd6be9b766b6ddd7e6de3cfe38e8baf27"},"revision